raspi-aarch64: package gpio.resource

The aarch64 package lists mbox, dma, sdio and bwfm out of the bcm2708 tree
and skips gpio, so on this target the platform has no pin-mux API at all --
the arm package has carried it since it existed. Nothing noticed because the
one driver that needs to mux pins, sdio.resource, reaches into GPFSEL3
itself.

That is the whole gap: the resource builds, and it is the only thing on the
platform that knows the BCM2712 routes GPIO through the RP1 instead.

diff --git a/arch/aarch64-raspi/boot/mmakefile.src b/arch/aarch64-raspi/boot/mmakefile.src
index fdd1c1dec2..d954e09fb0 100644
--- a/arch/aarch64-raspi/boot/mmakefile.src
+++ b/arch/aarch64-raspi/boot/mmakefile.src
